   "heuNote": "14 +/- 3 t. Produced at two gaseous-diffusion plants: Lanzhou (Plant 504, HEU from Jan 1964) and Heping/Jinkouhe (Plant 814, from 1970). Weapon HEU production is assessed to have stopped in 1987. China has never formally declared a halt.",
   "puNote": "2.9 +/- 0.6 t weapon-grade plutonium; weapon production ended ~1990-91. China's last INFCIRC/549 declaration (for 2016) reported only 41 kg of civil separated plutonium. That is changing fast: the 200 tHM/yr Jinta reprocessing plant began operating around mid-2025 and separates roughly 2 t of reactor-grade plutonium a year, with a second identical plant complete and a third under construction. IPFM estimates China…",
