  "narrative": "Israeli and US strikes in June 2025 hit Natanz, the Natanz pilot plant, Fordow and Esfahan, and analysts assess they destroyed or disabled essentially all of Iran's roughly 22,000 installed centrifuges at the three safeguarded enrichment sites. Further strikes followed in February 2026. The IAEA withdrew inspectors after June 2025 and, after 28 February 2026, stopped conducting verification activities under the NPT safeguards agreement; the Agency continues to report Iran in violation, with access denied to some 20 declared nuclear sites. Grossi assessed that most - but less than 70 percent - of the roughly half-tonne of 60 percent enriched uranium is inside the Esfahan tunnel complex, material that is technically about 99 percent of the way to weapon-grade by separative work. UN sanctions were re-imposed via snapback in September 2025. A June 2026 US-Iran memorandum of understanding commits both to negotiate a nuclear and sanctions deal within a nominal 60 days, extendable. Iranian officials have repeatedly threatened NPT withdrawal without executing it. The critical point for this atlas is causal: Saudi, Turkish and Egyptian officials have all conditioned their own restraint explicitly on Iran not fielding a weapon, so Iran's trajectory is the single largest determinant of whether a Middle East cascade begins.",
