  "assessment": "The archetypal latent state: a full civil fuel cycle including a completed reprocessing plant and roughly 44-45 tonnes of separated plutonium, paired with strong legal, political and normative barriers. HIGH-CONFIDENCE that Japan has no weapons programme; CONFIRMED that it holds the largest separated-plutonium stock of any non-nuclear-weapon state.",
  "breakout": "Carnegie's 2026 threshold study notes Japan has held the relevant technical capabilities since the 1970s and 'likely could develop nuclear weapons within a matter of months.' Reactor-grade plutonium and the absence of any weaponisation programme, test data or delivery integration argue for months-to-a-couple-of-years, not weeks.",
